WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:10.510
20. Bored But Never Boring Board games have a history of over 5,000

2
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:15.510
years. They've been found in ancient Egyptian tombs and are mentioned in documents from

3
00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:21.110
Old Rome and China. They're more popular now than ever before, though, with new games

4
00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:27.270
appearing alongside old favorites every year. The variety of modern board games is a big

5
00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:33.030
part of their appeal. Some require players to move along a path of spaces as directed

6
00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:39.550
by rolls of dice. Some, like Dominion, are actually card games with no board. Others

7
00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:45.910
offer very different challenges. Most older board games, such as Chess and Go, are designed

8
00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:52.510
for two players. Many newer games, however, can be enjoyed by larger groups. In Scrabble,

9
00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:57.910
two to four players must create words from tiles showing individual letters and point

10
00:00:57.910 --> 00:01:04.210
values to finish it. Monopoly allows up to eight players the chance to buy and sell property

11
00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:10.690
for play money. In Chinese Checkers, which is actually from Germany, two to six people

12
00:01:10.690 --> 00:01:17.150
jump over their own and each other's pieces to move across the board. And in Trivial Pursuit,

13
00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:23.150
teams answer questions on different topics to try to finish first. In recent years, a

14
00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:29.210
new generation of board games has become very popular. These designer games often feature

15
00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:35.910
themes such as the settling of land, katan, building of cities, citadels, and development

16
00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:41.710
of resources, karkasan. Social in nature, they are usually easy to learn and designed

17
00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:47.530
to keep all players in competition until the end. Of course, any board game requires a

18
00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:53.550
place to play and people to play with. Having trouble with that? No problem. Many board

19
00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:59.170
game stores rent games and tables to players, who may be complete strangers until they sit

20
00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:05.470
down together. So give Super Mario a rest and try a face-to-face contest against other

21
00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:09.270
humans. You just might find it a lot more fun.
